{
  "id": "cass-apartment",
  "name": "Cass's Apartment",
  "description": "Cass's room above the Tilt, up the staff door behind the bar: half bedroom, half the bar's storeroom, warm and untidy. Dark plank walls, pipes along the ceiling, worn floorboards. An unmade bed under a red blanket with a lamp on the night table, and above it an old photograph of her with her younger brother. A worn couch with a plaid throw faces a chunky old TV that only shows static. The one window looks out on the Ribbon's towers, a wall lamp beside it. On the right, the bar's spillover: crates of bottles, a dented keg, a box of glasses, a mop, her apron and a bar towel on hooks, a little sink with a kettle and mugs. In the corner, the narrow wooden door back down to the bar, under a small caged lamp. She works nights and sleeps through the day.",
